# {{name}}

{{title}}: a [pytacheck](https://github.com/thesanogoeffect/pytacheck) pack.

## Use it

```bash
pytacheck pack install ./{{name}}         # while developing (a live path pack)
pytacheck modules --pack {{name}}
pytacheck run paper.json --preset {{name}}  # this pack's "default" preset
```

In Python:

```python
import pytacheck as pc

out = pc.module_run(paper, "{{name}}::{{module}}")
```

## Develop it

* Modules are the `*.py` files in this folder (helpers start with `_`).
* `pytacheck pack check .` checks the pack the way the store's CI does.
* `pytest` runs the tests in `tests/`.
* Fill in the `<validation>` block of each module once you have validated it
  (and the `validation=` numbers), so users can see how well it works.

## Publish it

See "Publish to the store" in pytacheck's `docs/MODULES.md`: open a pull
request adding this folder to
[pytacheck-modules](https://github.com/thesanogoeffect/pytacheck-modules),
or list your own repository there with a `packs/{{name}}.json` entry.

